{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":10810,"output":9427,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":7044,"totalTokens":20237,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Let me go through each item.\n\nQ041: source \"Accept these selections\" (button to accept trap selections). target \"确认法术选择\" - \"confirm spell selection\". Context shows traps, not spells. \"these selections\" → \"法术选择\" adds \"spell\" and mistranslates traps as spells. Evidence: self.traps_selected, \"Preparing trap with normal trigger\", max_traps. FINDING: SUBJECT/VALUE — \"selections\" refers to traps; \"法术\" (spell) is wrong. Also \"确认\" vs \"Accept\" — acceptable. FINDING, claim_type SUBJECT, target_span \"法术选择\", correction \"确认这些陷阱选择\", evidence \"self.traps_selected[tid] = not self.traps_selected[tid]\".\n\nQ042: \"Got to level 10 of the infinite dungeon.\" → \"到达无尽地下城第10层。\" Correct. Empty candidates.\n\nQ043: \"THAT'S NOT A VERY HERMIT-LIKE ATTITUDE.\" → \"这可不像我这个隐士该有的态度。\" Hmm. Source is generic \"that's not a hermit-like attitude\" — not necessarily \"my\". Target says \"我这个隐士\" (my attitude as a hermit). The speaker is the hermit? Actually context: the speaker is a hermit-like character... The source \"THAT'S NOT A VERY HERMIT-LIKE ATTITUDE\" — ambiguous whose attitude. Target adds \"我这个\" (my). Could be ADDITION. Actually speaker is likely a hermit NPC commenting; \"that's not a very hermit-like attitude\" addressed to... Hmm. Actually the option label is spoken by the player? This is an answer option \"{_t\"[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]\", jump=\"competition\"}\" — player's reply to hermit NPC. So the hermit is the NPC, and target \"我这个隐士\" attributes hermit-hood to the speaker (player), which is wrong — REFERENT/SUBJECT. But can I tell from visible text that the speaker isn't the hermit? Context: the NPC says \"STILL CAN'T HEAR YOU... THE BROTHERHOOD...\" and player answers. In \"help\" chat, the NPC says \"I DON'T EVEN WANT THE ASS-CURE FOR ME\" — that's the hermit NPC speaking. The answer option is the player's line. The player isn't established as a hermit. The source is ambiguous though — it could be the player remarking \"that's not a very hermit-like attitude\" about the NPC's hoarding. Target \"这可不像我这个隐士该有的态度\" — \"this is not the attitude a hermit like me should have\" — attributing to self. Hmm, actually wait — could the target be reinterpreting? The source is in all caps — it's the player's response. Actually the player is responding to the hermit's rant; \"THAT'S NOT A VERY HERMIT-LIKE ATTITUDE\" — the player comments that the hermit's behavior isn't hermit-like. So \"我这个隐士\" is wrong referent. But is it certain? Evidence: the answer is player's line in response to hermit's complaint. I'd say FINDING REFERENT with moderate confidence, or UNCERTAIN. Evidence: \"_t\\\"[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]\\\", jump=\\\"competition\\\"\" appears after hermit's text \"I DON'T EVEN WANT THE ASS-CURE FOR ME.\" Actually that text is in the help chat, and the answer leads to competition. Hmm, the previous chat text is the proposal chat; the answer with source match is in help chat. I'll report UNCERTAIN REFERENT: target adds \"我这个\" making it first-person, while source doesn't specify whose attitude; the line is a player reply. Correction: \"这可不太像隐士的态度。\" I'll say FINDING? Rules: FINDING when evidence sufficient. The hermit NPC speaks in first person about himself; the option is the player's answer. Actually wait — is it possible the hermit says this line? The answers belong to the player. So \"THAT'S NOT...\" is player's line, referring to the NPC's attitude. Target changing to \"我这个隐士\" misattributes. But could the player be a hermit? No evidence. The source says \"THAT'S\" not \"MY\". I'll go FINDING, REFERENT.\n\nQ044: source \"Have 100 walls...\" target \"让淤泥巢穴中的 200 面墙变成敌对生物。\" 100 → 200. Clear VALUE FINDING. Evidence: \"Have 100 walls on the sludgenest turn into hostile creatures.\" Target span \"200 面墙\".\n\nQ045: \"But what is all th...\" → \"但是这一切到底是……\" Fine. Empty.\n\nQ046: \"Killed a Bringer of Doom.\" → \"杀死一名厄运行者。\" \"Bringer of Doom\" → 厄运行者 (\"Doom runner\"?) — 厄运 brings... \"Bringer\" = 带来者. \"厄运行者\" is a plausible translational name; hard to say objectively wrong. Could argue \"带来厄运者\" but \"厄运行者\" is a name choice; \"行者\" adds \"traveler\". Hmm. Rule 1: objective substantive defects. \"Bringer of Doom\" → \"厄运行者\" — the \"bringer\" meaning is lost, \"行者\" (walker) added. This is a VALUE issue arguably. But proper noun naming flexibility... I'd report UNCERTAIN VALUE: \"厄运行者\" 未体现 \"Bringer\"（带来者）含义。Actually I might just leave empty. Given ambiguity, maybe UNCERTAIN. Let me consider: is this \"objective\"? The translation changes \"bringer\" to \"walker/traveler\". I'll report UNCERTAIN.\n\nAlso \"a Bringer of Doom\" — an article, \"一名\" fine.\n\nQ047: source: \"...ruined from your fight with the creature carrying it.\" target: \"看来在你刚才和那个人类搏斗的时候被打碎了\" — \"那个人类\" (that human). Source says \"the creature carrying it\" — the creature carrying the paper. Target says human. Is that supported? The context: a Sun Paladin veteran's journal; the creature is a spider (arachnids, matriarch). So \"creature\" → \"人类\" (human) is wrong — the creature is a spider. But wait, is the \"creature carrying it\" the spider? The lore is about spiders in Ardhungol; the fight was with \"the creature carrying it\" — likely the spider. Visible evidence: context mentions arachnids, \"that spider is the matriarch here\". So \"那个人类\" contradicts... well, actually the fight just happened; the creature carrying the scraps. The journal writer was a Sun Paladin (human? elf?). Hmm — the creature carrying the paper: the player fought the creature. The creature is presumably the spider. Target says \"那个人类\" — human. That's a REFERENT error supported by context: spiders. But careful: is \"the creature carrying it\" definitely not human? The context is spider lore; the paper is carried by \"the creature\" which the player fought. Given context strongly indicates spiders, FINDING. claim_type REFERENT, target_span \"那个人类\", correction \"携带纸片的生物\", evidence \"the creature carrying it\" — but wait, evidence must be in source: \"ruined from your fight with the creature carrying it\" is in source. Good. Also \"被打碎了\" — \"ruined\" → 被打碎了 (smashed), fine-ish.\n\nAlso \"sun paladin\" in quotes → \"太阳骑士\" — fine.\n\nAlso target adds \"这种人\" vs \"species\" — fine.\n\nOne more: \"ineffective on species 'sun paladin'\" → \"在'太阳骑士'这种物种的身上被证明无效\" — fine.\n\nQ048: \"Records of Lorekeeper Hadak part three\" → \"博学者哈达克的记录，第三部分\" fine. Empty.\n\nQ049: source \"When you do a mouse gesture (right click + drag) a color coded trail is displayed.\" target: \"当你用右键拖动画出鼠标手势时，始终会显示彩色的轨迹提示。\" Adds \"始终\" (always). Source doesn't say \"always\". Is that ADDITION? The setting name is \"Display mouse gesture trails\" and status depends on hide_gestures — enabling means display always. The source text itself doesn't say \"always\". Adding \"始终\" is an addition not supported by source. But rule 3: \"新增但与可见证据相容、且无法由可见证据判错的具体信息，不构成缺陷。\" Is \"始终\" compatible? The setting toggles hide_gestures; when enabled, trails displayed. When disabled, presumably hidden except during gesture? Actually hide_gestures — hmm. The source says a trail is displayed when you do a gesture. \"始终会显示\" (always displayed) — could conflict: source implies trail displayed during gesture only. \"始终\" changes meaning to always display. I'd call FINDING ADDITION: \"始终\" not in source; source conditions trail on performing a gesture. Evidence: \"When you do a mouse gesture (right click + drag) a color coded trail is displayed.\" Hmm, but \"always display\" matches the setting name pattern... Other settings: \"Always display combat properties...\" That's a different setting. This one is \"Display mouse gesture trails\" with hide_gestures toggle. The source text does not say always. I'll mark FINDING ADDITION with correction removing 始终. Or UNCERTAIN? I think FINDING is defensible: the source explicitly conditions display on performing the gesture (\"When you do a mouse gesture...\"), which conflicts with \"始终会显示\" (always displayed). Actually — the setting is about whether to display trails; enabling displays them always (even not during gesture?). Hmm, hard. Given the conditional \"When you do\", I'll say UNCERTAIN to be safe? The instruction: UNCERTAIN only when evidence points to a problem but genuine ambiguity remains. There is genuine ambiguity here about intended meaning. I'll go UNCERTAIN ADDITION.\n\nQ050: Long fountain text. Target adds \"位于德斯镇\" (in Derth) — source doesn't mention Derth. Actually Angolwen fountain — lore name \"Angolwen Fountain\". Target says \"位于德斯镇\" (located in Derth)! That's wrong — the fountain is in Angolwen. Source_context: newLore id \"angolwen-fountain\", name \"Angolwen Fountain\". So \"德斯镇\" (Derth) is an ADDITION/REFERENT error contradicted by context. FINDING. target_span \"位于德斯镇\", correction remove or \"位于安格列文\", evidence \"name = _t\\\"Angolwen Fountain\\\"\" / \"id = \\\"angolwen-fountain\\\"\". Note rule: evidence must appear verbatim in source_context. \"name = _t\\\"Angolwen Fountain\\\",\" — yes it appears. Wait, actually is Derth where? In ToME, Derth is a town; Angolwen is the mage ring. The target translation added \"位于德斯镇\" — definitely contradicted. FINDING, ADDITION (or REFERENT). I'll use ADDITION with correction \"（你在此看到一座庞大而精致的喷泉\".\n\nAlso check \"her arms outstretched to welcome all\" → fine. \"a dwarf manipulating earthen runes\" fine. \"The runes and the fireball are not connected to anything, and float in a fixed position in the air\" → \"未与任何东西相连，却保持在空中的固定位置\" fine. \"a carving repeating along the border\" → \"反复雕着一行细小字样\" — \"一行\" (one line) vs multiple carvings repeating; minor. \"in small print\" fine. Carvings: three ALL ARE WELCOME lines + others; \"一行\" slightly off but minor; skip. Also \"LET THE ARCANE ONCE MORE BE A BOON AND NOT A BANE\" → \"愿奥术再度成为...助益，而非灾祸\" fine. \"MAY WE HAVE THE WISDOM TO ONE DAY REUNITE THE WORLD IN SAFETY AND ENLIGHTENMENT\" → fine. \"GATHER HERE IN PEACE TO DISCOVER AND PERFECT THE KNOWLEDGE OF HOW, AND WHEN, TO WEAVE THE WORLD'S FABRIC\" → \"探索并完善何时、如何编织世界织物的知识\" fine.\n\nQ051: source: \"If you bring me a gem and a ring, I can create a new ring imbued with the properties of the gem.\" target: \"如果你给我找来一颗宝石和一枚项链，我可以帮你把宝石的力量镶嵌到戒指里去。\" — \"a ring\" → \"项链\" (necklace/amulet)! Then \"戒指\" later. So \"项链\" is wrong, should be \"戒指\". VALUE FINDING. Evidence: \"If you bring me a gem and a ring, I can create a new ring\". Target span \"一枚项链\".\n\nAlso \"you need a quality ring to use a quality gem\" → \"你得寻找高品质的戒指来用于高品质的宝石\" — \"寻找\" (find/seek) added; minor, meaning roughly \"need\". \"need\" → \"得寻找\" — adds action \"search for\". Minor; could report but likely fine-ish. Also \"The original traits of the ring\" → \"这颗戒指\" — \"颗\" measure word odd but minor. Skip.\n\nQ052: \"But then where are they now if they won?\" → \"兽人是胜利了，但是现在他们又在哪里呢？\" Adds \"兽人\" (orcs). Subject addition. Context: chat about Sher'Tuls who fought gods. \"They\" refers to Sher'Tuls. Target adds \"兽人\" — Sher'Tuls are orcs (Sher'Tul = orc forebears). Is that compatible with visible evidence? Context says \"Those are Sher'Tuls?\" — no visible mention of orcs. Rule 3: new info compatible with visible evidence and can't be judged wrong by it — Sher'Tul is not stated to be orcs in visible text. But it can't be judged wrong either. Hmm — is \"兽人\" contradicting? Not contradicting visible evidence. Rule 3 says compatible additions are not defects. Since visible text can't establish Sher'Tuls are orcs, but also can't refute... Actually \"无法由可见证据判错\" — cannot be judged wrong. So it's not a defect. Skip. Otherwise fine.\n\nQ053: \"Fear not. Return in a few days, and I'll have everything prepared.\" → \"别害怕，几天后你回来，我肯定把一切都准备好了。\" — \"I'll have everything prepared\" is future (\"届时我会准备好一切\"); target \"我肯定把一切都准备好了\" reads as already prepared (perfective). TIMING issue, mild. Hmm. \"Return in a few days, and I'll have everything prepared\" = when you return, everything will be ready. Target could be read as \"by the time you come back I'll surely have everything ready\" — Chinese \"把一切都准备好了\" with \"几天后你回来\" context could be future. Ambiguous; skip or UNCERTAIN. Also \"your odds of surviving our portal attempt will go up drastically\" → \"这能大大提高你通过传送门时存活的几率\" fine. \"It opens the ruins of Telmur, which the men of Sholtar sealed many years ago\" → \"它可以打开泰尔玛废墟，那是多年前肖尔塔人封印的地方\" — \"the men of Sholtar\" → \"肖尔塔人\" fine. \"If you happen to find a text... return with it\" → \"请帮我带回来\" — \"帮我\" added, fine. \"不要害怕... 我肯定\" fine. I'd skip Q053 or report TIMING UNCERTAIN. Let me think: \"我肯定把一切都准备好了\" most naturally reads as present-perfect \"I have everything ready\" but with \"几天后你回来\" it reads \"when you return in a few days, I'll have everything ready\" — actually Chinese: \"几天后你回来，我肯定把一切都准备好了\" — this is a future-perfect reading, acceptable. Skip. Empty candidates.\n\nQ054: \"I cleared the room of death and all I got was this lousy achievement!\" → \"我清完\"死亡之屋\"后发现我只得到了这个无聊的成就！\" fine. Note \"Room of Death\" translated 死亡之屋 — desc says \"\\\"Room of Death\\\" in Vor Armoury\" — fine. Empty.\n\nQ055: \"The Right thing to do\" → \"放走鲜血大师才是正确的选择\" — \"放走鲜血大师\" = \"release the Blood Master\"! Achievement id RING_BLOOD_KILL, desc \"Did the righteous thing in the ring of blood and disposed of the Blood Master.\" So the achievement is for KILLING the Blood Master. Target says \"放走\" (let go/release) — DIRECTION/ACTION error, contradicted by context \"disposed of the Blood Master\". FINDING. Correction: \"杀死鲜血大师才是正确的选择\" or \"做正确的事：除掉鲜血大师\". target_span \"放走鲜血大师\". evidence: \"desc = _t[[Did the righteous thing in the ring of blood and disposed of the Blood Master.]]\" — need verbatim substring from source_context: \"Did the righteous thing in the ring of blood and disposed of the Blood Master.\" appears. Use that.\n\nQ056: source has \"realizing it's actually a human inside that hulking, worn armor.\" Target: \"才发现那副庞大而破旧的战甲里其实装着弗莉吉亚的弟弟。\" — \"a human\" → \"弗莉吉亚的弟弟\" (Fryjia's younger brother). Context: Fryjia says \"please forgive her behavior. You will understand when you meet her father.\" and Valfren... \"Valfren collapses... Father... #LIGHT_GREEN#*She stands silent*#WHITE# You win\" — so Valfren is Fryjia's father, not brother! Evidence: \"Father... \" she says after Valfren collapses. So the armored human is Fryjia's father (Valfren), not her brother. Target \"弗莉吉亚的弟弟\" contradicted by context \"Father... *She stands silent for a few seconds*#WHITE# You win\" following Valfren's defeat. FINDING, REFERENT. Correction: \"弗莉吉亚的父亲\" or just \"一个人类\". Evidence verbatim: \"Father... #LIGHT_GREEN#*She stands silent for a few seconds*#WHITE# You win, @playerdescriptor.race@.\" — must appear verbatim in source_context. Let me check: \"Father... #LIGHT_GREEN#*She stands silent for a few seconds*#WHITE# You win, @playerdescriptor.race@.\" Yes appears as \"Father... #LIGHT_GREEN#*She stands silent for a few seconds*#WHITE# You win, @playerdescriptor.race@.\\nYou have done well.\" Good.\n\nAlso \"弗……特……玛……尔……\" for \"f...t...ma....ll...\" — hmm, source letters f, t, ma, ll — likely \"fryjia's father\"? Actually it might spell something. Target 弗尔特玛尔. Fine-ish, skip.\n\nQ057: \"Reload/regenerate Zone and level\" → \"重新加载/重新生成地图和角色\" — \"level\" → \"角色\" (character)! Should be \"关卡/层级\". Debug menu: class ReloadZone reloads zone and level. \"level\" here is game level, not character. FINDING VALUE. Evidence: \"Reload/regenerate Zone and level\" (source). Correction: \"重新加载/重新生成区域和层级\". target_span \"地图和角色\".\n\nQ058: \"Lua inspect [Projectile]\" → \"即使此处没有抛射物，也可在 Lua 中查看 [抛射物]\" — big addition: \"even if there's no projectile here\". Context: \"if p and config.settings.cheat then list[#list+1] = {name=_t\"Lua inspect [Projectile]\"...}\" — the entry appears only when p (projectile) exists. So \"即使此处没有抛射物\" is contradicted by \"if p and config.settings.cheat\". FINDING ADDITION. Correction: \"Lua 查看 [抛射物]\". Evidence: \"if p and config.settings.cheat then list[#list+1] = {name=_t\\\"[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]\\\", action=\\\"debug-inspect\\\", color=colors.simple(colors.LIGHT_BLUE), actor=p} end\" — verbatim substring needed. I can use \"if p and config.settings.cheat then\" — that appears verbatim.\n\nQ059: \"Removed 89 beneficial effects from enemies via Disintegration.\" → \"必须单次使用裂解清除敌人身上的89个增益效果\" — adds \"单次\" (in a single use)! Source doesn't say single use. Context: can_gain increments self.nb per event, threshold >= 89 — cumulative counter, not single use. So \"单次\" is wrong: the achievement accumulates (\" / 89\" track). Evidence: \"self.nb = (self.nb or 0) + 1\\n\\t\\tif self.nb >= 89 then return true end\" — verbatim: \"self.nb = (self.nb or 0) + 1\" appears. FINDING ADDITION/CONDITION: \"单次\" contradicts cumulative counter. claim_type ADDITION (or CONDITION). I'll use ADDITION. Correction: remove \"单次\": \"使用裂解从敌人身上清除了89个增益效果\".\n\nQ060: \"Killed oneself as a halfling.\" → \"选择半身人种族并杀死敌人。\" — \"Killed oneself\" = suicide (id HALFLING_SUICIDE) → target says \"杀死敌人\" (kill enemies). DIRECTION/SUBJECT error. Evidence: \"Killed oneself as a halfling.\" and context id \"HALFLING_SUICIDE\". FINDING. Correction: \"以半身人身份自杀。\" target_span \"杀死敌人\".\n\nNow Q046 reconsider: \"Bringer of Doom\" → \"厄运行者\". I'll include UNCERTAIN VALUE. Actually is \"行者\" defensible? \"Bringer\" = 带来者; \"厄运行者\" reads as \"doom runner/walker\". It's a substantive mismatch in the name. But translation of proper names allows latitude... The rules say only objective defects. \"厄运行者\" doesn't convey \"bringer\". I'll report UNCERTAIN.\n\nQ043 reconsider verdict: FINDING vs UNCERTAIN. The evidence: the source line is an answer option (player's reply) following the hermit NPC's rant. Actually wait — which chat? The source match is in chat \"help\" answers, jumping to \"competition\". The help text is the hermit's plan to steal secrets. Player replies \"THAT'S NOT A VERY HERMIT-LIKE ATTITUDE.\" — commenting that the hermit's attitude (stealing, spite) isn't hermit-like. So the target's \"我这个隐士\" (me, the hermit) is a wrong referent — the speaker isn't the hermit. But is the player the hermit? The player is talking to the hermit (\"STILL CAN'T HEAR YOU\" — hmm that's proposal text; the hermit can't hear? weird). Anyway, visible evidence: the line is an answer option in a dialog where the other party says \"I DON'T EVEN WANT THE ASS-CURE FOR ME. I'M GOING TO STEAL EVERY SECRET...\" The answer responds to that. \"THAT'S\" points to the other's attitude. Target's first-person \"我这个隐士\" misattributes. I'll go FINDING, REFERENT. Hmm, but could the player character be a hermit too? No evidence. Actually risk: maybe the speaker of the option... answers are always player options. And \"THAT'S\" demonstrative refers to something else. FINDING.\n\nActually wait — reconsider: maybe the hermit is the NPC and the player says \"that's not a very hermit-like attitude\" — target \"这可不像我这个隐士该有的态度\" — could be the hermit speaking? No, it's an answer option. OK FINDING.\n\nHmm, but one more consideration: this dialog — the NPC is the hermit (Alchemist?). The player's line \"THAT'S NOT A VERY HERMIT-LIKE ATTITUDE\" mocks the NPC. Yes.\n\nQ049 verdict: I'll go with UNCERTAIN for 始终. Actually let me reconsider: \"始终会显示彩色的轨迹提示\" vs source \"When you do a mouse gesture ... a trail is displayed\". The Chinese says \"when you draw a mouse gesture with right-click drag, [always] a colored trail hint is displayed.\" Actually reading the Chinese fully: \"当你用右键拖动画出鼠标手势时，始终会显示彩色的轨迹提示。\" The \"始终\" could mean \"always (in the sense of consistently) when you do a gesture\" — i.e., every time. That reading is compatible. Hmm. \"始终会显示\" attached to the when-clause — \"whenever you do a gesture, a trail is always displayed\". That's compatible with source. So maybe not a defect. The \"提示\" (hint) addition is minor. I'll leave Q049 empty? Or UNCERTAIN. Given the reading ambiguity, \"始终\" most likely means \"consistently/each time\" here given placement after the time clause. I'll leave empty. Hmm, but it could also be read as \"always displays\". Rule 4: UNCERTAIN only when evidence points to a problem but genuine ambiguity. The ambiguity is genuine; evidence doesn't strongly point to a problem. I'll leave candidates empty with observation noting the possible ambiguity. Actually the schema requires observation min length 1; I can write a brief note.\n\nQ046: also consider \"杀死一名厄运行者\" — \"一名\" for a creature; fine.\n\nLet me also double-check Q041: \"Accept these selections\" → \"确认法术选择\". The dialog is about trap selection (traps_selected, max_traps, \"Preparing trap\"). \"法术\" (spell) contradicts trap context. FINDING SUBJECT/VALUE. I'll use claim_type SUBJECT with evidence \"self.traps_selected[tid] = not self.traps_selected[tid]\". Also \"these selections\" → \"法术选择\" loses plural \"these\"? minor. Correction: \"确认这些陷阱选择\".\n\nQ050: also check \"her arms outstretched to welcome all\" → \"她伸展双臂，欢迎所有人\" fine. Also target \"喷泉边缘反复雕着一行细小字样\" — \"a carving repeating\" — \"一行\" hmm skip.\n\nAlso Q050: check second finding? The \"德斯镇\" is main one.\n\nQ051 second: \"you need a quality ring to use a quality gem\" → \"你得寻找高品质的戒指来用于高品质的宝石。\" \"need\" → \"得寻找\" — adds \"寻找\" (find). Minor; \"你得\" = you must; \"寻找\" — \"you must find a quality ring\" vs \"you need a quality ring\". Adding \"寻找\" is mild. Skip? It changes \"have/need\" to \"search for\". Borderline; skip to be safe. Actually also \"There is a small fee dependent on the level of the ring\" → \"根据戒指等级我要收取一小笔费用\" fine.\n\nAlso Q051: \"The original traits of the ring will be lost\" → \"这颗戒指里面原来所有的属性会丢失掉\" — \"所有的\" (all) vs \"original traits\" — \"original traits\" → \"原来所有的属性\" adds \"all\". Minor. Skip.\n\nQ059 correction: source is past tense \"Removed 89 beneficial effects\" — target \"必须...清除\" changes to requirement \"must\". Hmm! Target: \"必须单次使用裂解清除敌人身上的89个增益效果\" — \"must clear 89 beneficial effects from enemies in a single use of Disintegration\". Source: \"Removed 89 beneficial effects from enemies via Disintegration.\" — past tense achievement desc. Target reframes as a requirement with 必须. That's another issue (ACTION/STATE). I'll report 单次 as the main finding and maybe include the 必须 rephrasing as second candidate. Two independent candidates: (1) ADDITION \"单次\"; (2) the desc rewritten as imperative requirement vs statement of accomplished fact — claim_type ACTION, target_span \"必须单次使用裂解清除\", correction \"使用裂解从敌人身上移除了 89 个增益效果\". Evidence for (2): \"Removed 89 beneficial effects from enemies via Disintegration.\" Both fine. But maybe keep just one to avoid overreach? Rule 5 encourages multiple independent candidates. I'll include both. Actually, achievement descriptions in ToME are typically statements of what was done; but some Chinese translations convert to requirement style... The source is declarative past. I'll include as UNCERTAIN for the 必须 one? Hmm. The counter track \" / 89\" supports cumulative. I'll make candidate 1 FINDING (单次), candidate 2 UNCERTAIN (declarative vs requirement). Actually, converting to \"必须\" changes it into a task description — many official translations do this. I'll mark UNCERTAIN.\n\nQ056: also \"弗……特……玛……尔……\" vs \"f...t...ma....ll...\" — target renders as 弗尔特玛尔; \"ll\" → 尔? \"ma\" → 玛, \"ll\" → 尔 — dropping one syllable? Eh, skip.\n\nQ053: leave empty.\n\nQ042, Q045, Q048, Q052, Q054: empty.\n\nNow count items Q041–Q060 = 20. Good.\n\nFor Q058 evidence verbatim check: source_context contains: \"if p and config.settings.cheat then list[#list+1] = {name=_t\\\"[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]\\\", action=\\\"debug-inspect\\\", color=colors.simple(colors.LIGHT_BLUE), actor=p} end\" — I'll use substring \"if p and config.settings.cheat then\" which appears verbatim. Also other entries like \"if a and config.settings.cheat then\" appear; using \"if p and config.settings.cheat then\" is specific to projectile. Good.\n\nQ057 evidence: \"Reload/regenerate Zone and level\" verbatim in source. Good.\n\nQ060 evidence: \"Killed oneself as a halfling.\" verbatim in source. Also context \"HALFLING_SUICIDE\". Use source text.\n\nQ055 evidence verbatim: \"Did the righteous thing in the ring of blood and disposed of the Blood Master.\" — appears within desc. Good.\n\nQ056 evidence verbatim: \"Father... #LIGHT_GREEN#*She stands silent for a few seconds*#WHITE# You win, @playerdescriptor.race@.\" — check exact characters: \"Father... #LIGHT_GREEN#*She stands silent for a few seconds*#WHITE# You win, @playerdescriptor.race@.\" Yes.\n\nQ044 evidence: \"Have 100 walls on the sludgenest turn into hostile creatures.\" — appears in source. Yes.\n\nQ047 evidence: \"ruined from your fight with the creature carrying it\" verbatim in source. Yes.\n\nQ041 evidence: \"self.traps_selected[tid] = not self.traps_selected[tid]\" verbatim. Yes.\n\nQ043 evidence: need verbatim. The answer: {_t\"[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]\", jump=\"competition\"}, — I'll use \"{_t\\\"[[SOURCE_MATCH_1]]\\\", jump=\\\"competition\\\"}\" which appears verbatim. And correction: \"这可不太像隐士的态度。\" Also claim REFERENT.\n\nQ050 evidence: \"name = _t\\\"Angolwen Fountain\\\",\" verbatim appears? In context: \"name = _t\\\"Angolwen Fountain\\\",\" yes. Also \"id = \\\"angolwen-fountain\\\",\". Use \"name = _t\\\"Angolwen Fountain\\\",\" — verbatim including comma. Yes it appears as `\\tname = _t\"Angolwen Fountain\",`. Good.\n\nQ051 evidence: \"If you bring me a gem and a ring, I can create a new ring imbued with the properties of the gem.\" verbatim in source. Good.\n\nQ059 evidence: \"self.nb = (self.nb or 0) + 1\" verbatim appears (in can_gain). Also \"if self.nb >= 89 then return true end\". Use the latter: \"if self.nb >= 89 then return true end\" verbatim. Good — supports cumulative threshold.\n\nQ046 UNCERTAIN: target_span \"厄运行者\", evidence \"Killed a Bringer of Doom.\", correction \"杀死一名带来厄运者／厄运使者\". Fine.\n\nNow Q049 observation: note that \"始终\" could read as \"every time\"; no candidates.\n\nWrite JSON."}}
